            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "the \"pick a file\" cases like `:wq`, `:caddfile`, etc., are the more interesting cases and is why I [mentioned](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/26472#issuecomment-4894996980) either a \"synchronous\" approach, or adding async support to those commands.\n\nso technically we haven't really addressed #26472 . but not sure if anyone actually uses this, though it would be a nice feature for plugins to use.\n\n`vim.ui.select()` exists, but it requires every plugin to feed in the list of files, whereas a \"dir browser\" is a generic concept that requires zero effort from plugins.",
